@@ -6751,7 +6751,7 @@ RVR_49=Enter at least one domain.
 RVR_50=Not a valid domain name:
 RVR_51=That list is too long for one object. Split it into two lists.
 RVR_52=A rule still uses this list. Delete it anyway?
-RABT_41=GOAT whisperer~
+RABT_41=GOAT Whisperer
 RVR_54=WireGuard targets need a hardware-acceleration bypass (the same one VPN Director uses). A source rule bypasses only that address; a destination or MAC rule bypasses the LAN, so LAN traffic loses hardware acceleration while such a rule exists. If the WireGuard client is down, whether the selected traffic is blocked or uses the WAN is set by the Killswitch of that client.
 RVR_57=Rules go live when you apply and are reverted automatically unless you keep them within the auto-revert timer (set on the Firewall page).
 RVR_58=IPv6 is covered: a destination list matches its IPv6 addresses and a MAC rule follows the device on both families. If the chosen tunnel carries no IPv6, that client's Killswitch decides whether the selected IPv6 traffic is blocked or uses the WAN.
